WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.388 --> 00:00:18.673
Henry his friends said good-bye to Nathan and Nora, and then hurried down the street toward the Martins'

2
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:23.654
house. On the way Henry explained how he'd realized that Marty was the thief.

3
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:26.955
"It's the only possibility," he said.

4
00:00:26.975 --> 00:00:30.836
"We already proved that none of our other suspects did it.

5
00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:33.937
Besides it makes perfect sense."

6
00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:35.318
"It does?"

7
00:00:35.818 --> 00:00:36.459
Cole said.

8
00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:39.060
"Sure," Henry said.

9
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.102
"Everyone else at the lemonade stand was distracted, remember?

10
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:46.184
Those two teenage girls were giggling together."

11
00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:47.925
Maggie grinned.

12
00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:52.067
"They were probably planning their shopping trip to the drugstore!"

13
00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.689
"Probably," Henry agreed.

14
00:00:54.709 --> 00:01:00.112
"And Ryan was busy chugging his lemonade and doing tricks with his skateboard."

15
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.321
"And I was talking to Nathan and Nora," Maggie remembered.

16
00:01:04.341 --> 00:01:06.022
"Even Mrs.

17
00:01:06.102 --> 00:01:09.463
Martin was distracted by her cell phone," Henry said.

18
00:01:09.483 --> 00:01:14.345
"While nobody was paying attention, Marty must have grabbed the cash."

19
00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:16.006
"And then what?"

20
00:01:16.366 --> 00:01:16.986
Cole asked.

21
00:01:17.006 --> 00:01:21.008
"Like Maggie said, there was too much money to hide in Nora's hands.

22
00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.589
And Marty's hands are even smaller."

23
00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:26.850
"He didn't need his hands," Henry said.

24
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.412
"He stuffed it in that toy suitcase he was holding."

25
00:01:31.272 --> 00:01:33.293
Maggie gasped.

26
00:01:33.753 --> 00:01:35.433
"Henry, you're a genius!"

27
00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:36.714
she shrieked.

28
00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.314
"It's the perfect hiding place!

29
00:01:40.155 --> 00:01:41.635
Why didn't I think of that?"

30
00:01:41.655 --> 00:01:45.536
"There was no reason to remember it," Henry pointed out.

31
00:01:45.556 --> 00:01:48.457
"Little kids always have toys, right?"

32
00:01:48.477 --> 00:01:50.297
"So how come you remembered?"

33
00:01:50.637 --> 00:01:51.378
Cole asked.

34
00:01:51.398 --> 00:01:54.719
"I didn't at first," Henry admitted.

35
00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:59.420
"But when Nora was talking about Marty, I started thinking about him.

36
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.522
That's when I remembered the suitcase and realized what must have happened."

37
00:02:05.362 --> 00:02:07.463
They had almost reached the Martins' house.

38
00:02:08.403 --> 00:02:09.504
Henry could see Mrs.

39
00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:11.205
Martin out in the yard with Marty.

40
00:02:12.145 --> 00:02:13.205
She saw them coming.

41
00:02:13.225 --> 00:02:16.447
"We were just about to go back to your house, Maggie!"

42
00:02:16.827 --> 00:02:17.607
she called out.

43
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:22.169
"I discovered something very interesting in Marty's suitcase."

44
00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:23.830
"You did?"

45
00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.391
Maggie hurried over.

46
00:02:26.311 --> 00:02:28.192
Henry and Cole were right behind her.

47
00:02:29.084 --> 00:02:31.885
Marty's suitcase was lying open in the front yard.

48
00:02:32.706 --> 00:02:34.046
Cash was spilling out of it!

49
00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:35.847
"My money!"

50
00:02:36.287 --> 00:02:37.408
Maggie cried happily.

51
00:02:37.428 --> 00:02:41.810
"So Marty was the thief," Cole exclaimed.

52
00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:43.951
Mrs. Martin smiled.

53
00:02:43.971 --> 00:02:47.532
"I just discovered Marty playing with all this cash.

54
00:02:48.332 --> 00:02:53.455
At first I couldn't imagine where it came from, but then I figured out what must have happened,"

55
00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:54.375
she said.

56
00:02:54.395 --> 00:02:56.256
"Sorry, Maggie.

57
00:02:57.168 --> 00:02:59.429
Marty likes to grab everything these days.

58
00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.791
He must have grabbed your money while I wasn't looking."

59
00:03:02.811 --> 00:03:07.134
"We just figured that out ourselves," Henry said.

60
00:03:07.154 --> 00:03:09.515
"Yeah," Cole chimed in.

61
00:03:09.535 --> 00:03:12.657
"Henry put together all the clues and solved the mystery."

62
00:03:12.677 --> 00:03:14.037
"You did?"

63
00:03:14.538 --> 00:03:16.078
Mrs. Martin looked impressed.

64
00:03:16.899 --> 00:03:17.959
"Good work, Henry.

65
00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.001
Maybe you'll be a police detective when you grow up."

66
00:03:21.861 --> 00:03:24.363
"It wasn't just me," Henry said.

67
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:26.204
"These guys helped."

68
00:03:27.396 --> 00:03:28.197
Cole grinned.

69
00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:30.718
"Yeah, solving mysteries is fun.

70
00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:35.702
It's sort of like solving the puzzles on the Puzzle Pirates website, only better."

71
00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.123
Mrs. Martin smiled back.

72
00:03:38.143 --> 00:03:41.245
"Well, keep up the good work," she said.

73
00:03:41.265 --> 00:03:47.349
"Now I'd better get Marty inside and explain to him why we don't steal other people's things.

74
00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.432
It would be awfully embarrassing to have to arrest my own son!"

75
00:03:51.452 --> 00:03:54.074
"Don't worry, Mrs.

76
00:03:54.154 --> 00:03:57.056
Martin." Maggie started gathering up her money.

77
00:03:57.852 --> 00:03:59.093
"I won't press charges."

78
00:03:59.974 --> 00:04:01.235
Mrs. Martin chuckled.

79
00:04:01.935 --> 00:04:04.037
Then she picked up Marty and went into the house.

80
00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.619
Maggie kept scooping up her money.

81
00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:08.280
Cole watched her.

82
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.242
"Aren't you going to share some of that with us?"

83
00:04:11.722 --> 00:04:12.743
he asked with a grin.

84
00:04:13.644 --> 00:04:14.384
Maggie looked up.

85
00:04:14.404 --> 00:04:16.626
"Share my money?"

86
00:04:17.106 --> 00:04:17.566
she said.

87
00:04:17.586 --> 00:04:19.568
"Why would I do that?"

88
00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:24.792
"Usually when people solve a mystery, they get a reward," Cole pointed out.

89
00:04:26.196 --> 00:04:28.298
Maggie didn't say anything for a second.

90
00:04:29.158 --> 00:04:30.979
She had a thoughtful look on her face.

91
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:32.861
"What's the matter?"

92
00:04:33.261 --> 00:04:34.101
Henry asked her.

93
00:04:34.121 --> 00:04:37.564
"Are you trying to figure out how much our reward should be?"

94
00:04:37.584 --> 00:04:40.005
"No," Maggie said.

95
00:04:40.025 --> 00:04:42.547
"But I am thinking about rewards.

96
00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:47.831
What if we turned the lemonade stand into a detective agency?

97
00:04:48.151 --> 00:04:51.293
That might be a faster way to earn money for my riding lessons!"

98
00:04:51.873 --> 00:04:52.794
Cole laughed.

99
00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.556
"The Lemonade Detectives?"

100
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:56.580
he joked.

101
00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.181
"Why not?"

102
00:04:58.581 --> 00:04:59.401
Maggie smiled.

103
00:04:59.421 --> 00:05:02.802
"We did a great job solving this mystery.

104
00:05:03.542 --> 00:05:07.143
We could solve other mysteries for people, and they could pay me."

105
00:05:07.163 --> 00:05:08.843
"Pay you?"

106
00:05:09.404 --> 00:05:10.064
Henry said.

107
00:05:10.084 --> 00:05:12.564
"Okay, okay.

108
00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:14.745
Pay us," Maggie said.

109
00:05:14.765 --> 00:05:18.306
"You guys could each get 10 percent of our rewards."

110
00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:20.867
Henry and Cole traded a look.

111
00:05:21.707 --> 00:05:24.408
Without a word they turned and started to walk away.

112
00:05:24.428 --> 00:05:27.401
"Wait!" Maggie ran after them.

113
00:05:27.421 --> 00:05:30.182
"I meant to say 15 percent."

114
00:05:31.403 --> 00:05:33.244
Henry and Cole kept walking.

115
00:05:33.264 --> 00:05:36.726
"Fine!" Maggie sounded annoyed.

116
00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:40.048
"We can split the money evenly."

117
00:05:40.068 --> 00:05:42.009
"That's more like it."

118
00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:44.410
Henry stopped and turned around.

119
00:05:45.371 --> 00:05:46.051
So did Cole.

120
00:05:46.071 --> 00:05:51.434
"If you throw in all the free lemonade we can drink, you have yourself a deal," he agreed.

121
00:05:51.454 --> 00:05:54.336
"Okay." Maggie nodded.

122
00:05:55.164 --> 00:05:56.345
"So let's have a cheer.

123
00:05:57.206 --> 00:05:59.648
Hooray for The Lemonade Detectives!"

124
00:06:00.728 --> 00:06:03.571
"Hooray!" Henry grinned.

125
00:06:04.391 --> 00:06:06.693
He liked the sound of The Lemonade Detectives.

126
00:06:06.713 --> 00:06:10.016
"Now all we need is another case!"
